## Langfuse adds guardrails that redact sensitive content before trace capture

Source: Langfuse — https://langfuse.com/changelog/2026-11-27-ai-gateway-guardrails
Published: 2026-11-27
Channel: news

Langfuse is an AI engineering platform that traces and evaluates model applications. Its AI Gateway now offers guardrails for sensitive content in requests and model responses. Teams can configure detection for personal information, secrets, prompt injection and custom patterns, or connect an existing Amazon Bedrock guardrail.

A matching rule can block traffic, replace sensitive text with a label, or log matches for monitoring. Langfuse says replacement happens before the content is forwarded or returned and before full trace capture. Rules can apply across an organization, or they can target particular users and API keys. A rule can cover the latest turn, the full input, the model output, or both. The announcement describes configurable controls. It does not report detection accuracy.

Why it matters: Teams capturing model traffic should check rule scope and test redaction with representative sensitive inputs before relying on the resulting traces.

