## Langfuse shares model pricing definitions across projects

Source: Langfuse — https://langfuse.com/changelog/2026-11-27-organization-model-definitions
Published: 2026-11-27
Channel: news

Langfuse is an AI engineering platform that traces model applications and helps teams measure their costs. Organization owners and administrators can now define model prices once for every project, rather than repeat custom definitions in each project. Shared definitions can use custom or negotiated rates, or start from a cloned Langfuse default.

When Langfuse resolves a model for cost inference, it checks project definitions first, then organization definitions, then Langfuse defaults. A team can clone an organization definition into a project to override it there. Organization definitions can also be synchronized through the Organization Models API. The project Models API now returns a scope field for each model and deprecates its earlier managed-model flag. The changelog does not claim that changing a definition alters provider billing.

Why it matters: Teams comparing inferred model costs across projects should check shared rates and any project overrides against their actual contracts.

